==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|imperfeccion}}. See {{prefix|im|perfection|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɪmpɚˈfɛkʃən/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛkʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{label|en|uncountable}} Those [[qualities]] or [[features]] that are imperfect; the characteristic, state, or quality of being [[imperfect]].
#: ''You can accept your '''imperfection''' or try to improve.''
# {{label|en|countable}} Something that makes something else less than perfect; a [[blemish]], [[impurity]], [[error]], etc.
#: ''He loves me despite my '''imperfections'''.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being imperfect}} {{l|en|corruption}}
* {{sense|something that prevents perfection}} {{l|en|fault}}, {{l|en|flaw}}, {{l|en|mark}}, {{l|en|problem}}, {{l|en|weakness}}
* See also [[Wikisaurus:defect]]

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|quality of being imperfect}} {{l|en|flawlessness}}, {{l|en|perfection}}

